WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:01.960
Welcome to Planet Earth.

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:07.470
She’s got the toughest streets around, and
if you’re not careful, that mean old missy

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:11.920
won’t hesitate to wash out her gutters with
your blood and decorate the sidewalks with

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:12.920
your teeth.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:18.680
It’s a tough world for the good and innocent,
with the looming shadow of crime lurking around

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:23.420
every corner, just waiting to prey on those
who are unable to defend themselves.

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:29.300
If you don’t have the tools to survive,
it’ll chew you up and spit you out like

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.590
a wad of stale chewing gum.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.940
That’s why we need a hero.

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:35.579
A dark defender.

00:00:35.579 --> 00:00:37.620
A cloak in the night.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:38.980
We need…

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:40.690
The Specter.

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:41.739
New Delhi, India.

00:00:41.739 --> 00:00:45.600
A woman walks home from her late-night job.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:51.200
She’s exhausted, she can feel the bone-deep
ache of fourteen hours on a factory line,

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:55.039
running herself ragged to support her three
kids back home.

00:00:55.039 --> 00:00:59.329
She can barely stand; can you really blame
her for wanting to take the shortcut down

00:00:59.329 --> 00:01:03.180
that dark alley, knowing it’ll shave fifteen
minutes off her trip?

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:08.899
She ducks in, clutching her purse tight and
keeping her head down, but it won’t do any

00:01:08.899 --> 00:01:09.899
good.

00:01:09.899 --> 00:01:12.130
A predator has been laying in wait.

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:17.450
He emerges from the darkness, wielding a huge
knife, and grabs her by the shoulder.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:21.649
He’s a few heads taller than her, with arms
thicker than her neck.

00:01:21.649 --> 00:01:26.390
He tells her to hand over the money she’d
spent all month working for, or he’d turn

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:28.490
her kids into orphans.

00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:34.119
His knife had tasted blood before and he’d
have no problem killing again.

00:01:34.119 --> 00:01:38.740
With tears streaking down her face, knowing
it’s futile to resist, she reaches out and

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:40.319
passes him the money.

00:01:40.319 --> 00:01:43.799
The bandit snatches it from her trembling
hand and snickers.

00:01:43.799 --> 00:01:45.189
Candy from a baby.

00:01:45.189 --> 00:01:49.599
He’s ready to turn around and make a run
with tonight’s takings when he feels an

00:01:49.599 --> 00:01:51.840
odd chill drift into the alley.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:53.969
A soft whoosh.

00:01:53.969 --> 00:01:57.039
He turns and sees a figure standing and watching
him.

00:01:57.039 --> 00:02:02.579
He’s tall and well-built, with a long, black
coat and a black wide-brimmed hat.

00:02:02.579 --> 00:02:09.149
He was darker than the dark: Light seemed
to disappear into him, a black shape against

00:02:09.149 --> 00:02:10.149
the background.

00:02:10.149 --> 00:02:11.340
It’s him.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:17.580
The man that all criminals know and fear,
all over the world, even if they’ve never

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:18.670
met him.

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:24.969
The intrusive thought, the moment of creeping
doubt that slithers into their minds the second

00:02:24.969 --> 00:02:27.159
they even contemplate breaking the law.

00:02:27.159 --> 00:02:29.680
The bad guys’ boogeyman.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:30.810
The Specter.

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:32.849
“Halt, evildoer!”

00:02:32.849 --> 00:02:34.689
the Specter commands.

00:02:34.689 --> 00:02:39.769
“You’ll return this fine lady’s money,
or you’ll suffer the consequences.”

00:02:39.769 --> 00:02:44.790
The bandit feels a tremor of fear quiver through
him, but he won’t back down.

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:45.790
Not yet.

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:52.900
He charges The Specter with his blade, slashing
like a madman, but not a single hit lands.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:57.329
The Specter weaves perfectly away from every
strike and effortlessly disarms the bandit

00:02:57.329 --> 00:02:59.799
with a perfectly-placed whack to the wrist.

00:02:59.799 --> 00:03:01.390
The knife clatters to the ground.

00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:06.760
He discombobulates the bandit with an open-palmed
strike to either side of his head, then knocks

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:09.359
him out with a laser-focused headbutt.

00:03:09.359 --> 00:03:14.489
He crumples to the ground, unconscious, and
The Specter breathes a sigh.

00:03:14.489 --> 00:03:15.890
Another battle won.

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:19.299
This whole time, the woman has been watching,
frozen in awe.

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:23.640
The Specter picks up her stolen money and
hands it back to her with a gentlemanly doff

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.019
of his wide-brimmed hat.

00:03:25.019 --> 00:03:28.239
He really is just darkness underneath.

00:03:28.239 --> 00:03:32.640
Unseeable, unknowable, a living shadow.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:37.150
She thanks him, and he assures her that it’s
all in a day’s work for a crimefighter like

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:38.150
him.

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:40.530
After all, somebody needs to do it.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:43.209
And in a flash of smoke, he’s gone.

00:03:43.209 --> 00:03:45.920
The woman makes it home safely that night.

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:46.920
London, England.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:50.069
A man lays beaten and bloody on the ground.

00:03:50.069 --> 00:03:54.109
Three assailants surround him, circling like
hungry wolves.

00:03:54.109 --> 00:03:58.250
One wields a long lead pipe, still slick with
the man’s blood.

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:02.930
Another, a switchblade, that he keeps clicking
in and out of the handle.

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:05.560
And the third carries a handgun.

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:09.450
The same handgun he’s used to take two lives
before.

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:15.030
The wounded man on the ground - with bruises,
cuts, a broken ankle, a broken wrist, four

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:19.489
broken ribs, and three missing teeth - is
desperate and afraid.

00:04:19.489 --> 00:04:22.720
He’s here because he was forced into a corner.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:27.860
He needed to borrow money from a dangerous
man tucked away in a dingy building in London’s

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:31.430
East End, the city’s organized crime epicenter.

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:35.860
The money he’d borrowed came with predatory
interest that he couldn’t pay back.

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:41.320
Now, he’s paying the difference in blood
to that same loan shark’s violent goons.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:46.110
The man with the gun, in a thick cockney accent,
tells him that this is why he shouldn’t

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:48.430
have messed around with Mr. Ford.

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:52.900
Now he’s going to be an example for anyone
else stupid enough to think they can stiff

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:56.830
the big man on a payment and live to tell
the tale.

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:59.880
He nods to the man with the pipe to finish
the job.

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:05.030
The beaten and bloodied man on the ground
closes his eyes as the goon steps closer,

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:10.419
lifting up the red-stained pipe and preparing
to finally cave his pitiful head in with it.

00:05:10.419 --> 00:05:16.199
In the dark, he hears the whoosh of the pipe’s
downswing, and the breeze hits his bruised

00:05:16.199 --> 00:05:18.500
cheek, but the pipe never connects.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:21.479
Instead, there’s a chorus of gasps.

00:05:21.479 --> 00:05:26.270
The man on the ground opens his eyes to get
a better look at what on earth has happened.

00:05:26.270 --> 00:05:33.380
A tall, dark man in a long, black coat and
a wide-brimmed hat is standing over him, holding

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:38.849
the lead pipe that he just easily snatched
from the hands of its previous user.

00:05:38.849 --> 00:05:40.759
The goons are all stepping back.

00:05:40.759 --> 00:05:42.669
The gunman raises his pistol.

00:05:42.669 --> 00:05:44.199
The other, his knife.

00:05:44.199 --> 00:05:46.220
All of them look afraid.

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:51.289
The man on the ground doesn’t know the stranger
who just saved his life, but in his presence,

00:05:51.289 --> 00:05:56.490
he feels something wash over him that he hasn’t
felt in a long while: Safety.

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:58.000
It’s him.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.690
It’s The Specter.

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:01.450
“You wretched villains.

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:06.240
Don’t you know better than to pick on the
weak, a bunch of ‘tough guys’ like you?

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:09.409
How about fighting someone your own size?”

00:06:09.409 --> 00:06:13.460
In a blind panic, the gunman raises his pistol
and fires.

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:16.060
The Specter moves like smoke in the wind.

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:18.500
He dodges the bullet and tosses the lead pipe.

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:22.919
It sails through the air and hits the gunman’s
skull with an almighty crack.

00:06:22.919 --> 00:06:25.530
He collapses, dropping his weapon.

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:29.640
The other two goons bum rush him, but it doesn’t
serve them any better.

00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:31.759
One slashes, the other punches.

00:06:31.759 --> 00:06:36.849
With a few skillful, fluid movements, he guides
one goon’s knife-wielding hand into the

00:06:36.849 --> 00:06:41.800
other’s shoulder, then disables both with
a pair of simultaneous chops to the throat

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:44.610
that Jackie Chan himself would be proud of.

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:49.750
All three goons are laid out on the ground,
either writhing and gasping or knocked out

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:50.750
cold.

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:55.720
The Specter straightens his coat and hat with
practiced finesse and returns to the man laying

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:57.050
on the ground.

00:06:57.050 --> 00:07:01.850
After checking that he was still alive and
conscious, he passed the man a wad of cash

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:05.759
and a phone, telling him to call an ambulance
and get his wounds treated.

00:07:05.759 --> 00:07:11.050
None of those men would ever bother him again,
and if they or any others dared to, then they

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:16.889
could expect to see the dark figure of The
Specter appearing behind them in their bathroom

00:07:16.889 --> 00:07:17.970
mirror.

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:23.800
After all, someone needs to be there to fight
crime, even when nobody else will.

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:25.840
New York City, USA.

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:28.689
Things are going sideways at a major bank
downtown.

00:07:28.689 --> 00:07:32.490
A group of well-armed, highly organized robbers
has broken in.

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:36.620
They’ve taken at least fifty hostages throughout
the building, and have informed the police

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:40.669
blockade outside that unless their demands
are met and they’re given free passage out

00:07:40.669 --> 00:07:44.560
of the building, they’ll start executing
people left and right.

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:49.180
And given the ruthless organization of this
particular criminal crew, it seems more than

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:52.840
likely that they’ll put their blood money
where their mouth is.

00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:57.820
Police squad cars form a horseshoe blockade
around the building outside, armed with handguns,

00:07:57.820 --> 00:08:00.259
shotguns, and assault rifles.

00:08:00.259 --> 00:08:04.320
Police snipers are finding their ideal perches
in the surrounding skyscrapers.

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:07.510
SWAT is on its way and a police helicopter
circles above.

00:08:07.510 --> 00:08:13.199
However, even if everything goes right, the
higher-ups know that some fatalities are basically

00:08:13.199 --> 00:08:14.199
inevitable.

00:08:14.199 --> 00:08:18.509
Crews of hardcore career criminals like this
wouldn’t go down without a fight.

00:08:18.509 --> 00:08:23.060
One way or another, some lives would be taken
today.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:27.630
Another transmission is delivered from the
inside after that: The robbers know that time

00:08:27.630 --> 00:08:31.069
isn’t on their side, so they’re flipping
the script.

00:08:31.069 --> 00:08:32.490
Five minutes, exactly.

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:37.820
If their demands aren’t met by then, blood
would be staining the bank’s immaculate

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:38.990
marble floor.

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:40.170
Tick tock.

00:08:40.170 --> 00:08:43.190
The negotiators on the front line are in a
cold sweat.

00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:44.190
Five minutes!?

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:45.190
No, that isn’t enough time.

00:08:45.190 --> 00:08:47.880
We can’t mobilize, it’ll be a massacre
in there!

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:52.190
How could ten greedy maniacs with assault
rifles pull the rug out from under them all

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:53.580
like this?

00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:56.620
Panicked thoughts swim through the head of
a sergeant heading the blockade.

00:08:56.620 --> 00:09:00.350
He can’t concede, his superiors would never
allow it.

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:05.070
Does he wait five minutes and see what happens,
or authorize his officers to breach the front

00:09:05.070 --> 00:09:10.310
doors, try to reclaim the bank, and potentially
create one of the worst bank robbery bloodbaths

00:09:10.310 --> 00:09:12.640
in New York City history?

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:15.380
Damned if he does, damned if he doesn’t.

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:19.110
And every second, the time to decide runs
out…

00:09:19.110 --> 00:09:22.020
That’s when he hears a soft whoosh behind
him.

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:27.210
Paranoid enough to jump at shadows, the sergeant
turns, reaching for his gun, and sees what

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:30.630
seems to be a dapper shadow standing right
behind him.

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:35.220
A tall man, with a long, black coat and a
wide-brimmed hat.

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:39.480
No face, just darkness itself under the shade
of the brim.

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:44.620
The stranger places a calm hand on his shoulder,
and suddenly, a sense of trust like he hasn’t

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:46.340
felt in years just sets in.

00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:51.710
Somehow, deep in his marrow, he knows this
man is here to help.

00:09:51.710 --> 00:09:55.010
“Rest assured, sergeant, everything is under
control now.

00:09:55.010 --> 00:09:58.010
For I, The Specter, have arrived to save the
day.

00:09:58.010 --> 00:09:59.670
How many criminals are inside?”

00:09:59.670 --> 00:10:02.410
The sergeant murmurs ten, in awe.

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:03.850
The Specter nods.

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:05.730
“Worry not, sergeant.

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:07.210
Nobody will die today.”

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:13.370
And with that, like the ghost that is his
very namesake, The Specter is gone.

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:16.270
Inside the bank, the leader of the robbers
checks his watch.

00:10:16.270 --> 00:10:19.700
Two minutes, and still no word from the cops
outside.

00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:21.750
He’s starting to lose his patience.

00:10:21.750 --> 00:10:27.380
A few unfortunate bank tellers and customers
crouch around him, their hands behind their

00:10:27.380 --> 00:10:28.380
heads.

00:10:28.380 --> 00:10:32.910
Five of his men are out here with him, armed
and keeping the situation under control.

00:10:32.910 --> 00:10:36.410
The other four have cracked the security on
the vault and they’re hauling out money

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:37.970
by the bagful.

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:40.340
And still, silence from the cops.

00:10:40.340 --> 00:10:45.570
He sneers, and the thought crosses his mind
that perhaps if he takes out a hostage or

00:10:45.570 --> 00:10:49.770
two now, the mooks out there might actually
take his threats seriously.

00:10:49.770 --> 00:10:51.330
That thought amuses him.

00:10:51.330 --> 00:10:52.760
Yeah, that’ll show ‘em.

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:55.080
They’ll finally know who they’re dealing
with here.

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:59.380
The leader shoulders his assault rifle and
draws a bead on the hostage sitting closest

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:00.380
to him.

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:04.240
Even his men are shocked by the suddenness
of it all, but they know better than to second

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:06.570
guess their boss at a time like this.

00:11:06.570 --> 00:11:09.550
He was always a little trigger happy…

00:11:09.550 --> 00:11:13.540
The hostage - an older gentleman who’d only
come into the bank to check his balance, cause

00:11:13.540 --> 00:11:17.700
he hadn’t figured out how to do it online
just yet - sees the gun and winces.

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:21.960
He survived ‘Nam, and this was how he was
going to go.

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:26.520
Gunned down on a Wednesday afternoon by some
creep for chump change.

00:11:26.520 --> 00:11:27.520
What a world.

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:32.890
The leader’s finger curls around the trigger,
but before he can complete a squeeze, an expertly-aimed

00:11:32.890 --> 00:11:38.070
fist collides with the back of his head, knocking
him unconscious in a single strike.

00:11:38.070 --> 00:11:41.370
The leader collapses, his rifle sliding across
the ground.

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:47.620
The Specter stands where he stood, straightening
his coat and blowing dandruff off of his knuckles.

00:11:47.620 --> 00:11:51.310
“Are you fellas ready to dance?” he growls.

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:55.350
He glides through them, moving with the grace
of a prima ballerina and hitting with the

00:11:55.350 --> 00:11:57.130
force of a freight train.

00:11:57.130 --> 00:12:00.880
The goons are down before any of them can
fire a single shot.

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:05.360
With the help of some quick-thinking bank
tellers, The Specter closes the vault door

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:09.870
from the outside, trapping the remaining four
robbers inside.

00:12:09.870 --> 00:12:12.240
Textbook crimefighting once more.

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:17.310
The bank customers and employees, weeping
with joy and relief, thank the Specter for

00:12:17.310 --> 00:12:18.910
saving their lives.

00:12:18.910 --> 00:12:22.060
He shakes his head and assures them it was
nothing.

00:12:22.060 --> 00:12:25.380
Just doing what he could, as any concerned
citizen should.

00:12:25.380 --> 00:12:29.990
He would have left after that, were it not
for one little problem.

00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:34.410
The NYPD has a number of employees at different
levels of their sprawling structure that are

00:12:34.410 --> 00:12:39.000
actually deeply embedded undercover agents
of the SCP Foundation.

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:40.820
And this isn’t a comic book.

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:45.391
There’s a word for when a mysterious man
made from darkness appears from nowhere, and

00:12:45.391 --> 00:12:50.420
effortlessly takes down ten heavily-armed,
highly-trained combatants by himself, and

00:12:50.420 --> 00:12:53.060
that word was “Anomalous.”

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:57.310
Knowing what this mysterious combatant was
capable of, the Foundation sends some of their

00:12:57.310 --> 00:13:02.080
best Mobile Task Force Operatives to apprehend
him, under the guise of just being standard

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:07.480
SWAT Team members sent in to get the situation
back under control in the aftermath of the

00:13:07.480 --> 00:13:08.480
robbery.

00:13:08.480 --> 00:13:13.760
However, much to their extreme surprise, The
Specter puts up absolutely no resistance to

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:14.760
them.

00:13:14.760 --> 00:13:19.170
He understands that the men here to apprehend
him are servants of law and order, and would

00:13:19.170 --> 00:13:22.550
not defy their will, but he pleads with them
to reconsider.

00:13:22.550 --> 00:13:26.560
“You don’t understand, sirs, you’re
making a huge mistake,” he says, distraught.

00:13:26.560 --> 00:13:28.360
“I’m here to help.

00:13:28.360 --> 00:13:32.960
I’m The Specter, defender of the innocent,
scourge of the evildoer.

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:34.000
You can’t lock me away!

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:35.000
You can’t!

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:37.800
The people need me!”

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:42.940
As tragic as it is to see a genuinely benevolent
anomaly beg for his freedom, the Mobile Task

00:13:42.940 --> 00:13:46.530
Force’s hearts have long since hardened
to this kind of thing.

00:13:46.530 --> 00:13:51.440
He wouldn’t be the first sapient humanoid
anomaly to speedrun all seven stages of grief

00:13:51.440 --> 00:13:55.270
on their knees in front of them, and he probably
wouldn’t be the last.

00:13:55.270 --> 00:14:00.190
Foundation protocol is to tag and bag either
way, even if they’d just used their anomalous

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:02.740
abilities to thwart a bank robbery.

00:14:02.740 --> 00:14:07.510
The Specter is hauled back to the nearest
Foundation Containment Site and held in a

00:14:07.510 --> 00:14:12.860
holding cell while researchers prepare to
conduct initial tests and questioning.

00:14:12.860 --> 00:14:18.490
Everything seems so run of the mill - Little
do they notice, something extremely strange

00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:22.950
is starting to happen to New York City beyond
the containment chamber’s walls.

00:14:22.950 --> 00:14:28.300
They’re about to learn the true, devastating
consequences of keeping a pure force of good

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:30.800
like The Specter locked up.

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:36.050
Like a switch has been flipped, nearby police
suddenly become oddly listless.

00:14:36.050 --> 00:14:40.750
Instead of working, they just chat with each
other and random citizens about the weather.

00:14:40.750 --> 00:14:45.100
Some watch SCP Explained on their phone while
active robberies are happening.

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:49.190
A man is mugged right in front of a squad
car and the cop inside just listens to his

00:14:49.190 --> 00:14:52.170
Van Halen CDs at max volume.

00:14:52.170 --> 00:14:56.850
In actual precincts, the on-duty cops start
to wonder why on earth they’re actually

00:14:56.850 --> 00:14:57.850
here.

00:14:57.850 --> 00:15:01.830
In this building, all together, listening
to phone calls from weirdly panicked people

00:15:01.830 --> 00:15:04.060
and typing up reports on…

00:15:04.060 --> 00:15:05.060
Stuff?

00:15:05.060 --> 00:15:07.420
It all just seems oddly confusing.

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:12.040
They decide to go outside and watch clouds,
or go home and play video games.

00:15:12.040 --> 00:15:16.890
It doesn’t make any sense that they’re
just standing around in here doing nothing,

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:18.600
for no reason.

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:21.730
Across the city, strange incidents start to
occur.

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:25.700
People who so much as knock into each other
while walking on the crowded New York streets

00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:31.070
begin to brawl with one another on the ground,
while nobody around them even really acknowledges

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:34.390
that they’re doing it, let alone tries to
break them up.

00:15:34.390 --> 00:15:38.950
Nearby, cars crash at the intersection, and
rather than getting out to exchange insurance

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:44.050
information, the irate drivers draw guns and
start to duel like bit-characters in an old

00:15:44.050 --> 00:15:45.640
cowboy movie.

00:15:45.640 --> 00:15:47.700
Nobody really seems to mind.

00:15:47.700 --> 00:15:52.030
As if noticing a change in the wind, organized
crime rackets decide that secrecy isn’t

00:15:52.030 --> 00:15:53.600
the way to go anymore.

00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:59.330
Mob enforcers rob stores and shake down random
people in the streets, taking wallets, watches,

00:15:59.330 --> 00:16:01.210
phones, and jewelry.

00:16:01.210 --> 00:16:05.170
Criminals break into people’s homes and
start ransacking the place, stealing everything

00:16:05.170 --> 00:16:11.400
from flat-screen TVs to priceless family heirlooms,
while their owners sit on the couch, seemingly

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:15.240
unable to even comprehend that something is
going wrong here.

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:19.240
But everything is still about to get a whole
lot worse.

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:22.010
The city breaks into riots and looting.

00:16:22.010 --> 00:16:23.750
People battling in the streets.

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:28.870
News helicopters circle above, reporting the
chaos unfolding below them, but they do so

00:16:28.870 --> 00:16:34.370
with an odd kind of detached calm, not really
comprehending the full scope of what’s happening

00:16:34.370 --> 00:16:35.830
or why.

00:16:35.830 --> 00:16:39.420
Just that a whole lot more is on fire now
than it was before.

00:16:39.420 --> 00:16:41.140
How strange.

00:16:41.140 --> 00:16:46.150
This is the moment when the SCP Foundation
realizes the meaning of The Specter’s pleading.

00:16:46.150 --> 00:16:53.140
He really was being entirely unselfish, because
you see, The Specter isn’t just an extremely

00:16:53.140 --> 00:16:58.200
devoted crime fighter, he’s the very personification
of the concept of fighting crime.

00:16:58.200 --> 00:17:03.760
He can’t ever be locked up or contained,
because if you do so, then the very concept

00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:07.339
of resisting crime fades from the human consciousness.

00:17:07.339 --> 00:17:10.640
Order ceases to be and chaos reigns.

00:17:10.640 --> 00:17:18.480
That’s why The Specter, also known as SCP-4494,
is classified as Archon - Meaning that he

00:17:18.480 --> 00:17:23.189
can’t be contained, because the danger of
containing him would be far greater than the

00:17:23.189 --> 00:17:26.899
danger of letting him roam around and do his
thing unhindered.

00:17:26.899 --> 00:17:32.799
He maintains an amicable relationship with
the SCP Foundation after everything that happened,

00:17:32.799 --> 00:17:36.570
willing to swoop in and help their agents
when they’re in a bind, and need a little

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:38.450
hand from a true hero.

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:44.620
And when he’s not fighting crime, he relaxes
in The Specter Cave by watching TV and playing

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:45.620
video games.

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:48.370
No, we’re not making that up.

00:17:48.370 --> 00:17:53.019
Unsurprisingly, his favorite video games are
ones where you get to play as superheroes,

00:17:53.019 --> 00:17:57.490
though he will occasionally indulge in some
Grand Theft Auto V - Just don’t expect him

00:17:57.490 --> 00:18:01.610
to break any traffic laws while he’s playing,
thank you very much.

00:18:01.610 --> 00:18:06.289
So if ever you feel afraid, or that the dark
forces that are all too human in this world

00:18:06.289 --> 00:18:10.769
are marshaling against you, know this: You
don’t fight alone.

00:18:10.769 --> 00:18:14.630
There’s a man in the shadows, ready to come
to your aid.

00:18:14.630 --> 00:18:16.740
He’s a warrior for justice.

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:18.980
He’s a defender of the innocent.

00:18:18.980 --> 00:18:21.909
But most of all, he is…

00:18:21.909 --> 00:18:23.669
The Specter.

00:18:23.669 --> 00:18:26.990
Now go check out “SCP-999 Tickle Monster
VS.

00:18:26.990 --> 00:18:32.900
the Most Evil SCPs” and “SCP-999 and the
Most Wholesome SCPs” for more anomalies

00:18:32.900 --> 00:18:34.770
that really just want to make the world a
better place!

